"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at improving email management efficiency by developing AI models to summarize emails based on specific instructions. The project kicked off in Q3 2023 with Marcus Cole as the leader, focusing on optimizing cloud storage and leveraging AI for data visualization. Key developments include securing a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research, reaching a major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, and updating security protocols to include multi-factor authentication and encryption. The project budget has been adjusted to $550,000, with specific allocations for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). The team is currently gathering innovative ideas from R&D, with proposals due by July 20th, and is working on features that summarize emails based on user instructions."
